---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { PROJECTS } from "../consts";
import "./prose.scss";
---

<Layout
	title="Community & Contributing"
	description="One shared way to contribute, report issues and start discussions across every Dravia Vemal open source project."
	type="article"
>
	<main class="prose">
		<h1>Community &amp; contributing</h1>
		<p class="subtitle">
			The same friendly process works for every project — pick the repo,
			follow the steps below.
		</p>

		<h2 id="ways-to-help">Ways to help</h2>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>Star</strong> a project on GitHub — it genuinely helps.</li>
			<li><strong>Report bugs</strong> or request features via issues.</li>
			<li><strong>Ask questions</strong> and share ideas in Discussions.</li>
			<li><strong>Contribute code</strong> or docs with a pull request.</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Sponsor</strong> to fund maintenance and unlock a
				commercial license — see <a href="/versioning#licensing"
					>licensing</a
				>.
			</li>
		</ul>

		<h2 id="per-project">Project channels</h2>
		<p>
			Issues, discussions and pull requests live on each project's own
			GitHub repository:
		</p>
		<table>
			<thead>
				<tr>
					<th>Project</th>
					<th>Issues</th>
					<th>Discussions</th>
				</tr>
			</thead>
			<tbody>
				{
					PROJECTS.map((project) => (
						<tr>
							<td>
								<a href={project.docs}>{project.name}</a>
							</td>
							<td>
								<a
									href={`${project.repo}/issues`}
									target="_blank"
									rel="noopener"
								>
									Open issues
								</a>
							</td>
							<td>
								<a
									href={`${project.repo}/discussions`}
									target="_blank"
									rel="noopener"
								>
									Start a discussion
								</a>
							</td>
						</tr>
					))
				}
			</tbody>
		</table>

		<h2 id="contribution-workflow">Contribution workflow</h2>
		<p>
			All projects share the same <a href="/versioning#branching"
				>branching model</a
			>. Contributions target the <code>alpha</code> branch:
		</p>
		<ol>
			<li>Fork the repository and create a branch from <code>alpha</code>.</li>
			<li>
				Make your change with clear, focused commits (e.g.
				<code>feat: add waterfall chart</code>).
			</li>
			<li>Add or update tests and docs where relevant.</li>
			<li>
				Open a pull request against <code>alpha</code> describing the
				change and the motivation.
			</li>
		</ol>

		<h2 id="reporting-issues">Reporting a good issue</h2>
		<p>A useful bug report usually includes:</p>
		<ul>
			<li>The project and version (stable or alpha) you're using.</li>
			<li>A minimal, reproducible example.</li>
			<li>What you expected vs. what happened.</li>
			<li>Your OS, language/runtime and toolchain versions.</li>
		</ul>

		<h2 id="conduct">Be excellent to each other</h2>
		<p>
			Please keep interactions respectful and constructive. Harassment or
			hostility isn't welcome in any project space.
		</p>

		<h2 id="contact">Direct contact</h2>
		<p>
			For commercial licensing or private matters, reach out at
			<a href="mailto:contact@draviavemal.com">contact@draviavemal.com</a>.
		</p>
	</main>
</Layout>
